{"title":"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd97515c4454e1dd60f79f65fae79067c0a2d65a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1, n_2, \\dots , n_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"11\" /> be integers where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c45a9440a903bd7c6cff6b0be3105608f3cd9e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> is odd. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/388724cccbe0fe5a9485731145a67adabfdac72f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = (x_1, \\dots , x_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> denote a permutation of the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de3f952dc795872af257c44c72b2309528d64bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, \\cdots , m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8c54175b10521f76ebeab4bef74fba00b0b76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x_1n_1 + x_2n_2 + ... + x_mn_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />. Show that for some distinct permutations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> the difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29e5e03addffdb2c35eac7579be58a7bbe43aabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a) - f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9d913109f09f79aa0f9b8182f420dd409b69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m!$\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916e1315b721b685c733a990a221051adebe3478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0,1,2,...,m!-1\\}\\not=\\{f(1),f(2),f(3),...,f(m!)\\}\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"466\" height=\"18\" /> then by the pigeon hole princible, there must be some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb0261f05f0175dcfc20a6eb34f5303823d18e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\in\\{1,2,...,m!\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/66930de24efb662f8a19bec4a7cd7962f9e59c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)\\equiv f(b)\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" /> as desired.  Thus, we must prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916e1315b721b685c733a990a221051adebe3478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0,1,2,...,m!-1\\}\\not=\\{f(1),f(2),f(3),...,f(m!)\\}\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"466\" height=\"18\" />.  Suppose there was such a situation.  Then, since the two sets have the same number of elements, for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1037befcbe2886b30f0d29464754bc42cadcfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\in\\{0,1,...,m!-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />, there exists a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c1df63728b57cbd6782a31e7d11cd31c54452c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v\\in\\{1,2,...,m!\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406215e692b1c373c3fbbfce9c838695d67501e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\equiv f(v)\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />.  So, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c1de2dd12ebbda5a820ff3e3a0300f978b2174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t\\equiv f(v_t)\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />.  Consider the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c20cd629f9362bea49b0902bf3f8cad64df83b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(v_0)+f(v_1)+\\cdots+f(v_{m!-1})\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />.  Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0247229b649ba0196d7739479f0eb56752f25b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(v_t)\\equiv t\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, we find the sum is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e345af6fe23a7b3b7d8e8928f9fe65a84891ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0+1+\\cdots+m!-1=\\frac{m!(m!-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"272\" height=\"38\" />.  \n</p><p>On the other hand, using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11dc3d039e46694d51ecf04e1670e6879cf596c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x_1n_1 + x_2n_2 + ... + x_mn_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />, we can combine the terms with the same coefficient (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb75ccf06e046206cb4c636a54d7be11d049fbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />).  For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, since all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/42628ab5952aa041b3649af187c7f256cfb4fe9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> are distinct, the coefficient in the sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39fd15b88b82971345fa815cf3eee987cafd21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"43\" height=\"25\" /> over all permutations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24acdf771030a87288dbdaabe6f7e0be14e50ea8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,...,m\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, the coefficient would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d435446a202f8865ed1858706244a5cb6e43c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^m i(m-1)!=\\frac{m!(m+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"210\" height=\"48\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e674a915f7587b4d52831f4237acb29ea2339d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m+1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" /> is an integer, so the coefficient is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5878dba16ddd471e5fc9ce4b7a3fb1e2720379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, the whole sum is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5878dba16ddd471e5fc9ce4b7a3fb1e2720379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1c9ade85486f8a764ef406e53ffed5e7f52311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m!(m!-1)}{2}\\equiv0\\pmod{m!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"207\" height=\"38\" />.  But, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c45a9440a903bd7c6cff6b0be3105608f3cd9e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9d913109f09f79aa0f9b8182f420dd409b69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m!$\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is even, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73b70b111e1d11e2d8e131944b1412b6a2a90c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m!-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> is odd.  Therefore, the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffdacb98df1a2790f220f7b4977b09a21493e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m!(m!-1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> has one factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9d913109f09f79aa0f9b8182f420dd409b69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m!$\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> does.  Contradiction!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef3a32260276575510a0549bfc248b011814d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b08c31f30ceb918a7d33da9b05d591cd8127486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,...,m\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877bae8499dbf5f070a78dab023af1fe9e9e5c98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g: S_m \\rightarrow \\mathbb{Z}_{m!}, g(x) = f(x) \\mod m!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"282\" height=\"20\" />. The problem is equivalent to showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not a bijection. Suppose by contradiction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> was bijective. Then since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe48ebca5554e89a543caf83ff1f92d9c992aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists y \\in S_m, f(y) \\equiv \\frac{1}{2}f(n+1,...,n+1) \\mod m!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"362\" height=\"38\" />. But then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/d/cfd2321ff0b76103266878c570187ffd0b362bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(y) \\equiv f((n+1,...,n+1)-y) \\mod m!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"321\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e15becf26582b3fcbc0b9676b80e8d9218e8be46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,(n+1,...,n+1)-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" /> are two distinct permutations in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/f/7ef3a32260276575510a0549bfc248b011814d63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" />. A contradiction.\n</p><p>(Not an original solution. See <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c6h17454p119174\">[1]</a> where others found the same solution).\n</p><p>~not_detriti \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO\" title=\"2001 IMO\">2001 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175356\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 283/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9132/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.997      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.997      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7333:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017175356 and revision id 285914. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}